BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//Karachi to Kashmir and Back//Itinerary//EN
CALSCALE:GREGORIAN
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:day1-karachi-kashmir@syed-bilal-faheem-portfolio
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260926
SUMMARY:Day 1: Out of the South
DESCRIPTION:Karachi falls away in the dark. Ten hours north\, the Indus catches the morning light at Sukkur for a short breakfast stop\, then it's on toward the capital\, arriving well after sunset.
LOCATION:Karachi -> Sukkur -> Islamabad
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:day2-karachi-kashmir@syed-bilal-faheem-portfolio
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260926
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260927
SUMMARY:Day 2: Into the Neelum Valley
DESCRIPTION:The road narrows and starts to climb\, threading past waterfalls and a river that marks a border. By evening the valley opens into Sharda\, ringed by pine and the first real mountains of the trip.
LOCATION:Islamabad -> Sharda
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:day3-karachi-kashmir@syed-bilal-faheem-portfolio
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260927
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260928
SUMMARY:Day 3: Where the Road Runs Out
DESCRIPTION:Taobat sits at the edge of the map\, the last village before the Neelum River bends out of Pakistan. A late breakfast in Sharda\, then hours deeper into the valley.
LOCATION:Sharda -> Taobat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:day4-karachi-kashmir@syed-bilal-faheem-portfolio
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260928
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260929
SUMMARY:Day 4: Higher Still
DESCRIPTION:A day with no destination but altitude\, up to Taobat Bala's meadows and back down again\, with the river for company the whole way.
LOCATION:Taobat -> Taobat Bala -> Taobat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:day5-karachi-kashmir@syed-bilal-faheem-portfolio
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260929
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260930
SUMMARY:Day 5: The Meadow Above the Clouds
DESCRIPTION:No road reaches Arang Kel\, only a footpath up through pine forest to a wooden village strung across an open meadow\, wrapped in cloud by evening.
LOCATION:Taobat -> Arangkel
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:day6-karachi-kashmir@syed-bilal-faheem-portfolio
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Day 6: Turning South
DESCRIPTION:One last morning in the meadow before the long haul begins\, down from the mountains and south across the plains toward Multan.
LOCATION:Arangkel -> Multan
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:day7-karachi-kashmir@syed-bilal-faheem-portfolio
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Day 7: City of Saints
DESCRIPTION:A night landing in the City of Saints\, its shrines and skyline waiting for a morning light this itinerary won't quite catch.
LOCATION:Arrive Multan
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:day8-karachi-kashmir@syed-bilal-faheem-portfolio
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261002
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261003
SUMMARY:Day 8: The Final Stretch
DESCRIPTION:The longest single leg of the trip\, breakfast in Multan\, then the plains sliding past\, with the Lansdowne Bridge at Sukkur as the last landmark before the coast comes back into view.
LOCATION:Multan -> Karachi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:day9-karachi-kashmir@syed-bilal-faheem-portfolio
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261003
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261004
SUMMARY:Day 9: Back to the Sea
DESCRIPTION:A built-in cushion day\, if Day 8 runs long\, this is where it lands. By eleven at the latest\, the Arabian Sea again.
LOCATION:Arrival in Karachi
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
